  "releaseNotes": "fix(SQL): PSDO-2940 - revert the SQL provider from Microsoft.Data.SqlClient back to System.Data.SqlClient 4.9.1. Microsoft.Data.SqlClient requires a loose native Microsoft.Data.SqlClient.SNI.x64.dll that failed to load in the consumers' single-file (Costura) deploy (DllNotFoundException 0x8007007E when connecting to Prod DB). System.Data.SqlClient has SNI built in, restoring the previous known-good connect path. Product code is a pure namespace swap; all connection/encryption behaviour (Encrypt, TrustServerCertificate, SqlCredential) preserved.\n\nfix(SQL): PSDO-2874 - treat the INSERT variant of the FK_SystemSetting_SystemSettingType violation as ignorable in ExecuteSqlQueryNoReturn's known-error allowlist, alongside the ALTER TABLE variant that was already tolerated. The settings-snapshot sync (TestValueInject.InjectStoredSettings) INSERTs SystemSetting rows from a newer-schema snapshot into an older/downgraded target DB whose SystemSettingType parent lacks those SettingIDs, producing SqlException 547. It is ignorable: the statement terminates (only the new-row INSERT rolls back; the UPDATE of existing settings already applied), which is the desired downgrade outcome. Previously this fell through to the catch's final else and raised a false-positive AutomatedError/Trello card; it is now a no-op like its ALTER-TABLE sibling.",
